# PORTVALD parity case table.
# Format: case_id|validate_type|input_value|description
# input_value is used verbatim and is moved into LS-INPUT-VALUE PIC X(50):
#   left justified, space filled on the right, truncated beyond 50 bytes.
# Leading and embedded spaces are therefore significant; trailing spaces are not.
# An empty input_value field means LS-INPUT-VALUE is all spaces.
#
# -- dispatch: values of LS-VALIDATE-TYPE outside I A T M -----------------
DSP-01|X|PORT1234|unknown validation type letter
DSP-02|i|PORT1234|lowercase i is not the I condition name
DSP-03| |PORT1234|blank validation type
DSP-04|1|1234567890|numeric validation type
DSP-05|a|1234567890|lowercase a is not the A condition name
DSP-06|m|1000.00|lowercase m is not the M condition name
#
# -- 1000-VALIDATE-ID ------------------------------------------------------
ID-01|I|PORT1234|documented happy path: PORT prefix plus 4 digits
ID-02|I|PORT0000|prefix plus four zeros
ID-03|I|PORT9999|prefix plus four nines
ID-04|I|PORTABCD|prefix plus alphabetic suffix
ID-05|I|XXXX1234|wrong prefix
ID-06|I|PORT|prefix only, suffix is spaces
ID-07|I|port1234|lowercase prefix
ID-08|I|PORT 123|embedded space inside the four digit suffix
ID-09|I|PORT12345|five digit suffix
ID-10|I|PORT123|three digit suffix
ID-11|I||all spaces
ID-12|I| PORT1234|leading space shifts the prefix
ID-13|I|PORT1234EXTRA|trailing junk after a valid looking id
ID-14|I|PORT+123|signed suffix
ID-15|I|PORT-123|negative looking suffix
ID-16|I|PORT111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111|input longer than 50 bytes, truncated on the move
#
# -- 2000-VALIDATE-ACCOUNT -------------------------------------------------
AC-01|A|1234567890|documented happy path: 10 digit account number
AC-02|A|11111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111|50 digits, fills LS-INPUT-VALUE completely
AC-03|A|00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000|50 zeros, numeric but equal to ZEROS
AC-04|A|0000000000|10 zeros
AC-05|A|ABCDEFGHIJ|alphabetic account number
AC-06|A||all spaces
AC-07|A|9999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999A|49 digits with one alphabetic byte in position 50
AC-08|A| 123456789|leading space
AC-09|A|12345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890|50 mixed digits
AC-10|A|1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111|49 digits, byte 50 is a pad space
AC-11|A|999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999|51 digits, truncated to 50 digits on the move
AC-12|A|1234567890-|trailing sign character
AC-13|A|+1234567890|leading sign character
AC-14|A|00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000001|50 digits, differs from ZEROS in the last byte
#
# -- 3000-VALIDATE-TYPE ----------------------------------------------------
TY-01|T|STK|valid: stock
TY-02|T|BND|valid: bond
TY-03|T|MMF|valid: money market fund
TY-04|T|ETF|valid: exchange traded fund
TY-05|T|stk|lowercase
TY-06|T| STK|leading space
TY-07|T|STKX|valid code with trailing junk
TY-08|T||all spaces
TY-09|T|OPT|three letter code that is not in the list
TY-10|T|Stk|mixed case
TY-11|T|BNDBND|code repeated
TY-12|T|ETF                                        X|valid code with junk beyond the compare length
#
# -- 4000-VALIDATE-AMOUNT --------------------------------------------------
AM-01|M|1000.00|typical amount
AM-02|M|0|zero
AM-03|M|-500.25|negative amount
AM-04|M|9999999999999.99|VAL-MAX-AMOUNT exactly
AM-05|M|-9999999999999.99|VAL-MIN-AMOUNT exactly
AM-06|M|99999999999999.99|14 integer digits, one more than the field holds
AM-07|M|1000.999|third decimal digit
AM-08|M|ABC|non numeric text
AM-09|M||all spaces
AM-10|M|1,000.00|thousands separator
AM-11|M|12.3-|trailing sign
AM-12|M| 42|leading space
AM-13|M|.75|leading decimal point
AM-14|M|0.001|third decimal digit on a sub cent amount
AM-15|M|1234567890123456789012|22 digits
AM-16|M|$100|currency symbol
AM-17|M|1E3|exponent notation
AM-18|M|+ 250.50|sign separated from the digits by a space
AM-19|M|5 +|sign after the digits
AM-20|M|1.|decimal point with no fraction digits
AM-21|M|-.5|signed leading decimal point
AM-22|M|0000000012.34|leading zeros ahead of the significant digits
AM-23|M|,5|leading thousands separator
AM-24|M|1111111111111.99|13 integer digits and two decimals, inside the range
AM-25|M|AB123456789012345|letters ahead of surplus integer digits are skipped with them
AM-26|M|AB12345X|letter reached because there are no surplus integer digits to skip
AM-27|M|1234567890123.99XX|bytes beyond a full receiving field are never examined
AM-28|M|123456789012345X67|letter reached after the surplus integer digits are skipped
AM-29|M|1.23X|letter after the fraction is already full
AM-30|M|1.2X|letter while the fraction still has room
AM-31|M|1.2.3|second decimal point
AM-32|M|4 2|space embedded between digits
AM-33|M|00000000000000000000042|21 leading zeros ahead of the significant digits
AM-34|M|1234567890123456.78|16 integer digits and two decimals
